Z||000000||phillip||03-31-2000||11:08 PM||||<BR>in case anyones interested and near the lou. ky. area i looked (briefly) at an '88 formula. on a buy here-pay here lot  that dosen't have the best rep (jim browns), but it looked pretty good. 5-speed, red,didn't have the formula sticker but i'm assumiming thats what it is ( could have been a 2.5 with dual exhaust switch) $3900 but dealer said he'd take $2900 (without haggling). not really what i want but might be worth watching. <BR> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by phillip (edited 03-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||04-01-2000||12:23 AM||||I'd have to check, but I believe All 88's have dual exhaust. I think you'd have to run the VIN to be sure it's formula if it's not marked. ((I'll have to dig out the 88 VIN data tomorow. I don't know if the online VIN decoders have that or if you can even tell from the VIN. Maybe I'll just print all the VIN pages. I've heard some people have questions about the decoders. This would settle that. [No, can't post it. Copy Rights.]))<P>2900 is alot unless it's in extreamly good shape, or a real formula. (It could be a formula that got painted. Look for repaint signs. They are always present in all but the very best jobs.)<P>It would have to be in very good shape. I turned down a 86.5 GT that a dealer near Pennsgrove,NJ wanted over 2 grand for. It was a repaint. Not a very good one. Ran OK, but didn't drive it. (battery bad. never move a car with a bad bat. To easy to get stuck on road if it stalls. I know. had it happen exactly once.) Had other problems. Probly still there or junked.......... <P>In a way I'd like a GT, but the 87SC I have is suprisingly quick. Plus I have a hard enough time seeing to park with the notchback. the FB GT is even worse. you can't really see much thru those sails even when they are clear.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 04-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||04-02-2000||12:32 AM||||The '88 4-cyl. coupe only has one exhaust tip....the drivers side.  The coupe and Formula rear bumpers are the same though, so coupes have dual cutouts on the bumper cover. ||||reg||1
